               <msContents>
                  <msItem class="#historica" n="1" xml:id="MS_Selden_Supra_31-item1"> <locus from="5">(fol. 5)</locus>
                     <title key="work_10915" type="desc">'Chronica mendosa Sarracenorum' to 683 A.D.</title>
                     <note>Latin translation by <persName key="person_296465262" role="trl">Robert of Ketton</persName>
                     </note>  <rubric>Chronica mendosa Sarracenorum</rubric>
                  <incipit type="prol.">Summa tocius heresis</incipit><incipit type="prol.">Cum iubendi religio parendique</incipit>
                     <incipit type="text">In creacionis sue primordio</incipit>
                     <note>At fols. 10v, 11 in the margin is a table of Roman, Hebrew, Egyptian, Greek, Persian, and Arabic months (13th cent.).</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem class="#historica #theologica" n="2" xml:id="MS_Selden_Supra_31-item2"><locus from="16">(fol. 16)</locus>
                     <title key="work_11444">De generacione Mahumet</title>
                     <rubric>de generacione Mahumet et nutritura eius quern transtulit Hermannus Sclavus </rubric>
                     <incipit>Liber generationis Mahumet nuncii Dei</incipit>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem class="#theologica" n="3" xml:id="MS_Selden_Supra_31-item3"><locus from="23v">(fol. 23v)</locus>
                     <title key="work_11580">Doctrina Mahumet</title>
                     <rubric>Doctrina Mahumet . .. ab eodem Hermanno translata</rubric>
                     <incipit>Erat nuncius Dei</incipit>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem class="#theologica" n="4" xml:id="MS_Selden_Supra_31-item4"> <locus from="32">(fol. 32)</locus>
                     <title key="work_12470">Koran</title>
                     <note>Latin translation by <persName key="person_296465262" role="trl">Robert of Ketton</persName>
                     </note>
                     <note>The Koran in Latin, with a 'Prefacio Roberti translatoris ad dompnum Petrum Cluniacensem abbatem in libro legis Saracenorum quem Alchoran uocant (text beg. 'Misericordi pioque Deo uniuersitatis creatori'), and notes: at end are three colophons, (1) 'Explicit Liber legis diabolice Saracenorum ...', (2) 'Illustri ... Petro Cluniacensi abbate precipiente suus Angligena Robertus Ketenensis librum istum transtulit anno Domini. M°. c°. xl°. iij°...', (3) a third which belongs to an Epistola Saraceni cum responsione Christiani (see fol. 5) which is not here: it states that Petrus Cluniacensis abbas got Petrus Toletanus, aided by Petrus (Pictavensis), to translate the work from Arabic into Latin in the year when Alfonso (viii) took Choria (Coria in Spain, i.e. A.D. 1141-3). </note>
                     <incipit>Misericordi pioque Deo uniuersitatis creatori</incipit>
                     
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
